cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "FraudShield: reference implementation and experiments for real-time fraud detection on PaySim"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Fatayo"
    given-names: "Michael Akorede"
    affiliation: "Department of Computer Science, Lead City University, Ibadan, Nigeria"
repository-code: "https://github.com/mafatayo/fraudshield"
license: MIT
version: "1.0.2"
date-released: "2026-10-11"
abstract: >-
  Code and results behind the MSc thesis "Development of a Fault-Injected Reference Implementation of a
  Real-Time Fraud-Scoring Pipeline for Mobile Money Transaction Streams, with an Evaluation on PaySim" (Lead City University). It contains a runnable, fault-injectable
  reference implementation of an idempotent transaction-scoring pipeline (partitioned log, decision store,
  apply-once state store, keyed alerts), the feature scheme, and the experiments on the PaySim dataset:
  two evaluation protocols, five seeds, a feature-group ablation, threshold-free metrics and latency benchmarks.
keywords:
  - fraud detection
  - mobile money
  - streaming
  - idempotent processing
  - fault injection
  - XGBoost
  - PaySim
